# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321 and the XOAUTH2 initial-response format
# (user=\x01auth=Bearer <token>\x01\x01, base64). Not a recording: phase-0
# capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# The credential is a bearer token and the preference list leads with PLAIN.
# PLAIN is offered, but it does not fit a token, so the client selects XOAUTH2.

S: 220 smtp.example ESMTP ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-AUTH PLAIN XOAUTH2
S: 250 OK
C: AUTH XOAUTH2 dXNlcj1hZGFAZXhhbXBsZS5jb20BYXV0aD1CZWFyZXIgeWEyOS5zM2NyM3QtdG9rZW4BAQ==
S: 235 2.7.0 Accepted
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 go ahead
C: Subject: hi
C:
C: hi
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
